7. CREATE FRONTEND - index.html
============================================================
Open the frontend folder and create index.html.

Write:

------------------------- index.html -------------------------

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>AI Price Prediction</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h2>AI House Price Prediction</h2>

    <input type="number" id="area" placeholder="Enter area">
    <button onclick="predict()">Predict</button>

    <h3 id="result"></h3>

    <script>
        async function predict() {
            let area = document.getElementById("area").value;

            let response = await fetch("/api/predict", {
                method: "POST",
                headers: {"Content-Type": "application/json"},
                body: JSON.stringify({area: area})
            });

            let data = await response.json();

            document.getElementById("result").innerText =
                "Predicted Price: " + data.predicted_price + " lakhs";
        }
    </script>
</body>
</html>

-----------------------------------------------------------

EXPLANATION:
- HTML creates the webpage.
- Input accepts the house area.
- Button sends the area to the AI model API.
- The result is displayed on the webpage.

============================================================
8. CREATE NGINX CONFIGURATION
============================================================
Open the nginx folder and create default.conf.

Write:

------------------------- default.conf -------------------------

server {
    listen 80;

    location / {
        root /usr/share/nginx/html;
        index index.html;
    }

    location /api/ {
        proxy_pass http://model-api:5000/api/;
    }
}

-----------------------------------------------------------

EXPLANATION:
Nginx displays the frontend webpage and forwards API requests to the AI model container.

============================================================
9. CREATE DOCKER COMPOSE FILE - compose.yaml
============================================================
Go to the main docker-ai-compose folder.

Create compose.yaml and write:

------------------------- compose.yaml -------------------------

services:

  db:
    image: postgres:16-alpine
    environment:
      POSTGRES_DB: aidb
      POSTGRES_USER: aiuser
      POSTGRES_PASSWORD: pass123
    volumes:
      - dbdata:/var/lib/postgresql/data
    healthcheck:
      test: ["CMD-SHELL", "pg_isready -U aiuser -d aidb"]
      interval: 5s
      timeout: 5s
      retries: 10

  model-api:
    build: ./model
    depends_on:
      db:
        condition: service_healthy

  frontend:
    image: nginx:alpine
    ports:
      - "8080:80"
    volumes:
      - ./frontend:/usr/share/nginx/html:ro
      - ./nginx/default.conf:/etc/nginx/conf.d/default.conf:ro
    depends_on:
      - model-api

volumes:
  dbdata:

-----------------------------------------------------------

SIMPLE EXPLANATION:
- db: Creates the PostgreSQL database container.
- model-api: Builds and runs the AI model container.
- frontend: Runs the Nginx frontend container.
- ports: Opens the webpage on port 8080.
- volumes: Stores database information and shares the frontend files.
- depends_on: Starts the database before the AI model.

