============================================================
13. IMPORTANT DOCKER COMPOSE COMMANDS
============================================================

Start all containers:

docker compose up -d

Build and start:

docker compose up --build -d

Check containers:

docker compose ps

View logs:

docker compose logs

Stop and remove containers:

docker compose down

Restart containers:

docker compose restart

IMPORTANT:
The database volume is kept when you run docker compose down.
To delete the database data as well, run:

docker compose down -v

Do not use -v when you need to keep saved records.

============================================================
14. COMMON ERRORS
============================================================
1. Docker is not running:
   Open Docker Desktop and wait until the engine starts.

2. Website is not opening:
   Run docker compose ps and check that frontend is running.

3. Port 8080 is busy:
   Change "8080:80" to "8081:80" in compose.yaml.
   Then run docker compose up -d.
   Open http://localhost:8081.

4. Database connection error:
   Check whether db is healthy:

   docker compose ps

   View database logs:

   docker compose logs db

5. Python code changed:
   Rebuild the model container:

   docker compose up --build -d model-api

